WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.714
A signed JWT carries claims plus a signature;
its readable payload is not encrypted merely

00:00:05.714 --> 00:00:10.984
because it is signed. A service needs a
validation policy: trusted issuer and keys,

00:00:10.984 --> 00:00:16.317
permitted algorithms, intended audience, token
type and applicable time constraints.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.698
A valid signature alone does not establish that
this token belongs at this API or that its

00:00:21.698 --> 00:00:24.008
subject may access the requested record.

00:00:24.008 --> 00:00:29.482
Access and refresh tokens have different roles.
Short access-token lifetimes limit exposure,

00:00:29.482 --> 00:00:34.896
while refresh-token rotation or sender
constraints address renewal risk. Revoking a
refresh

00:00:34.896 --> 00:00:39.953
token does not magically invalidate every
already issued self-contained access token.

00:00:40.008 --> 00:00:45.531
Central issuance with local verification can
reduce repeated authentication calls, but

00:00:45.531 --> 00:00:50.541
introduces key-distribution and revocation
tradeoffs. OAuth concerns delegated

00:00:50.541 --> 00:00:56.256
authorization; OpenID Connect adds
authentication conventions. Neither is
synonymous with

00:00:56.256 --> 00:01:02.036
the JWT data format. If a user’s refresh token
is revoked, must a locally validated access

00:01:02.036 --> 00:01:04.027
token stop working immediately?

00:01:04.027 --> 00:01:09.070
No. Immediate rejection requires an additional
mechanism such as introspection or a

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:14.112
revocation/version check; otherwise the access
token may remain valid until expiry.

00:01:14.112 --> 00:01:19.624
A service should expose only necessary
interfaces and run with limited privileges. Non-
root

00:01:19.624 --> 00:01:25.076
execution, reduced capabilities, a read-only
filesystem where feasible and narrowly scoped

00:01:25.076 --> 00:01:30.286
workload credentials reduce consequences of
compromise. Secrets should be managed with

00:01:30.286 --> 00:01:34.708
explicit access, rotation and revocation rather
than hardcoded in source.

00:01:34.708 --> 00:01:40.108
Environment variables and mounted files each
have exposure tradeoffs; a secret store still

00:01:40.108 --> 00:01:42.448
needs authentication and authorization.

00:01:42.448 --> 00:01:48.484
Input handling must match the destination.
Parameterized database operations separate data

00:01:48.484 --> 00:01:54.654
from SQL, contextual output encoding protects
HTML contexts, and destination validation plus

00:01:54.654 --> 00:02:00.690
network controls help constrain outbound URL
requests. An ORM can still execute unsafe raw

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:01.227
queries.

00:02:01.448 --> 00:02:06.596
Error handling should avoid disclosing internal
details while retaining useful protected

00:02:06.596 --> 00:02:11.510
diagnostics. Trust forwarded identity or IP
information only from configured trusted

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:16.540
intermediaries, and order middleware so identity
and permission decisions occur before

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:21.922
protected work. Can a service trust X-Forwarded-
For simply because the request contains that

00:02:21.922 --> 00:02:22.331
header?

00:02:22.448 --> 00:02:27.958
No. Clients can supply headers. The trusted
proxy path must overwrite or validate forwarded

00:02:27.958 --> 00:02:32.196
information, and network address still does not
prove user permission.

00:02:32.196 --> 00:02:37.546
The supplied Uber case distinguishes tabletop
exercises, red-team operations and smaller

00:02:37.546 --> 00:02:43.138
repeatable simulations. These methods test
different things: decision-making and
escalation,

00:02:43.138 --> 00:02:48.731
broader adversary behavior, or focused detection
and response. The historical example should

00:02:48.731 --> 00:02:52.317
not be treated as a statement of Uber’s current
procedures.

00:02:52.317 --> 00:02:57.526
For this course, a tabletop preserves the
architectural learning without running intrusion

00:02:57.526 --> 00:02:59.610
tools or accessing real credentials.

00:02:59.817 --> 00:03:05.507
Assign roles for triage, service ownership,
communications and decision authority. Introduce

00:03:05.507 --> 00:03:11.135
synthetic evidence in stages: suspicious token
use, an unexpected outbound connection, then

00:03:11.135 --> 00:03:16.515
an unavailable dependency. Ask what evidence is
needed, what can be contained and which

00:03:16.515 --> 00:03:17.690
users are affected.

00:03:17.817 --> 00:03:22.567
Record timing and assumptions, then conduct an
after-action review with owners for

00:03:22.567 --> 00:03:27.781
improvements. Coverage mapped to ATT&CK
techniques can reveal gaps, but a checked box
does

00:03:27.781 --> 00:03:30.851
not prove that a control will detect every
variation.

00:03:30.851 --> 00:03:36.401
If a simulation triggers an alert, is the
response process necessarily successful? No.

00:03:36.401 --> 00:03:42.273
Someone must triage it, coordinate decisions,
contain harm and recover; the exercise should

00:03:42.273 --> 00:03:43.886
test that complete chain.
